  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "If I have vive trackers plugged into my computer, VRChat recognizes them (or at least one of them) and spawns a tracking ball at the center of my playspace on the floor. This happens even if the trackers are disabled in SteamVR and the lighthouses are turned off.\nAdditional Information: I use vive trackers and lighthouses in conjunction with my Oculus Rift to have full body tracking. But I can't open up VRChat in Steam if my trackers are charging, because VRChat will recognize them and force me to calibrate (which just makes my avatar crumple to the floor).",
